<speak>That is probably the safest way for me to tackle it. If I try to make every decision on the spot, I stop halfway and the room looks worse than when I began. We might do one drawer at a time. The business has made me used to large projects with lists and deadlines, but at home that approach can become too much. My daughter says I shouldn't need a project plan to tidy a shelf. She's right, although I maintain that a small label is perfectly reasonable.</speak>